quran[8]{c,v,t}:
  8,62,"And if they intend to deceive you, Allah is surely enough for you. He is the One Who strengthens you (directly) through His help and through the believers (who follow you)."
  8,63,"And He united their hearts (in mutual compassion). Had you spent all that is on the earth, you could not have united their hearts, but Allah has united them (despite their long history of conflicts and hostilities). Allah is indeed All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  8,64,O (Esteemed) Prophet! Sufficient for you is Allah and those of the believers who follow you (steadfastly).
  8,65,"O (Esteemed) Prophet! Urge the believers to fight (in self-defence). If there be twenty steadfast among you (in the event of war), they shall overcome two hundred (combatant enemies). And if there be one hundred of you, they shall overcome one thousand (combatant enemies) from among the disbelievers because they are a people who do not understand."
  8,66,"Now Allah has lightened your burden, for He knows that there is (some degree of) weakness in you. So, if there are one hundred steadfast among you, they shall overcome two hundred (combatant enemies). And if there are one thousand (steadfast) among you, they shall overcome two thousand (combatant enemies) by Allah’s permission. And Allah is with the steadfast."
  8,67,"It is not for a prophet to take prisoners of war until he has completely conquered the battlefield. (O people!) You desire the (temporary and lower) gains of this world, while Allah desires (for you the permanent and superior reward of) the Hereafter. And Allah is All-Mighty, All-Wise."
  8,68,"Had it not been a prior decree (of forgiveness) from Allah, a severe torment would have come upon you for what you had taken (as spoils from the battle or the ransom of prisoners)."
  8,69,"So (from now on), consume the spoils you have acquired, for they are lawful and fine. And be conscious of Allah. Indeed, Allah is Most-Forgiving, All-Merciful."
